{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>A serpent of copper.</b> Once he understood the intent of his Maker, he agreed to make it of copper and not of gold, in order that it remind them of their sin by its material appearance, its name, and its form — for they did the deed of the serpent through the vanity of their lips, speaking against HaShem, against His work, and against His servant."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:40:28.590619987Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}